## Ruling content (body review)
Ordering in `- decision:` (explicit, first→fifth):
1. satisfies-vs-implements FIRST — no `implements` field; contract realization stays `satisfies` by authoring convention
2. fields admitted — `component` and `uses` only, on `codeAnchor`
3. value form — `component?: ComponentAnchorId`, `uses?: readonly CodeAnchorId[]`; no free strings / detached enums
4. validators — target existence; endpoint types/namespaces; one-level membership (impl:/api: → component:); unique + non-empty-when-present uses; unique edges; self-ref refused; multi-node cycles are DATA not findings
5. census — always generated from graph + runtime constants; never hand-maintained; empty-state honesty

ADR three-part (all in `- rationale:`):
- hard to reverse — anchor API + edge vocabulary become contracts
- surprising without context — realization stays `satisfies`; cycles accepted; structural edges confer no realization state
- real trade-off — two narrow fields vs rejecting implements/inference/lifecycle/open tags
- cautionary evidence — gen-1 taxonomy drift via reviews/14

Refusal list present IN Spec body (consequence bullets):
- new fields extend `codeAnchor` only; no per-namespace sibling builders
- new edges are anchored claims only, never inferred; imports not architecture; no fourth claim
- anchors carry no intent/readiness/status/delivery fact; memberOf/uses mint no delivery facts and do not change readiness floors
- no free-form tag vocabulary, authored lifecycle, or parallel registry
- foreign fields remain extraction errors; closed envelope; malformed structural field refuses whole anchor
- anchor-required lint remains warn-level and optional

